 "model_b_CC_source": {
  "source": "Connes-Consani, Geometry of the scaling site (alainconnes.org/wp-content/uploads/scalingsite.pdf), Sec 4-5.2",
  "deg": "deg(D)=sum_j h_j, h_j in H_j=lambda_j H_p (order = jump of derivative, scaled by lambda: log-coordinate slope jump)",
  "Lemma5.7_arithmetic_Fr^a_mu(f)(l)=mu f(l/mu), all mu in R*_+": "points H->mu H (translation on log circle), orders x mu, deg x mu",
  "Lemma5.8_relative_Fr^r_h(f)(l)=f(hl), h in H_p^+": "points H->H/h (translation), deg preserved",
  "Lemma5.9_absolute_Fr_h(f)=h f, h in H_p^+": "points fixed, deg x h; Fr_h = Fr^a_h o Fr^r_h",
  "consequence": "mu-multiplicity on C_p exists honestly but only for the R_max-SEMILINEAR arithmetic Frobenius; the R_max-linear point map (relative) has degree 1. For mu=p^k, Fr^a_{p^k} = absolute Frobenius (fixes every point of C_p).",
  "bidegree_obstruction": "a real-weight 1-cycle supported on a translation graph in C_p x C_p has tangent direction (1,1) so fibre-bidegree (c,c); it cannot have bidegree (1,mu) for mu!=1."
 },
